      "quote": "The objective of this systematic review and meta-analysis was to evaluate the pooled efficacy and safety of high-dose versus low-dose thromboprophylaxis for VTE in hospitalized patients with COVID-19.",
      "reason": "The review objective is explicitly stated (evaluate pooled efficacy and safety of high- vs low-dose thromboprophylaxis for VTE in hospitalized COVID-19 patients). However, the statement is not presented using a structured question-formulation framework (e.g., explicit PICO phrasing), so it only partially meets the requirement to use a relevant question-formulation framework."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "The objective of this systematic-review and meta-analysis was to compare the efficacy and safety of high-dose versus low-dose thromboprophylaxis in hospitalized patients with COVID-19.",
      "reason": "For an intervention review, the planned comparison is clearly stated: population (hospitalized patients with COVID-19), intervention (high-dose thromboprophylaxis), comparator (low-dose thromboprophylaxis), and outcomes (efficacy and safety, with primary efficacy outcome VTE and primary safety outcome major bleeding described elsewhere in the text). This supplies the elements of a PICO-style comparison."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 85
}

{
