    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "MEDLINE and EMBASE were searched from January 2020 up to October 2021 for RCTs comparing different regimens of venous thromboprophylaxis in hospitalized adult patients with COVID-19. ... RCTs including hospitalized patients with objectively diagnosed SARS-CoV2 infection and comparing high-dose anticoagulation (experimental group) with low-dose anticoagulation (control group) were eligible. Studies with a non-randomised design or published in languages other than English were excluded.",
      "reason": "The eligibility criteria specify population (hospitalized adult patients with COVID-19), study design (RCTs), interventions (high- vs low-dose anticoagulation) and the search date range, but do not comprehensively report other study characteristics used for eligibility such as settings details, required follow-up duration, or all question-framework components."
